(3040869, 422322, 45003, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulieG:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a great image.  Congrats on your blue.  I was just wondering.  I love what you did with the colors and I see that you mention that you cross processed it.  Is that what gave it the cool colors and how do you do that?  I''d appreciate any info.  Thanks. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yep, the cross process filter gave these colors. The cross process filter is one of the Nik Color Efex pro filters.</td>', 'Originally posted by JulieG: This is a great image.  Congrats on your blue.  I was just wondering.  I love what you did with the colors and I see that you mention that you cross processed it.  Is that what gave it the cool colors and how do you do that?  I''d appreciate any info.  Thanks.   Yep, the cross process filter gave these colors. The cross process filter is one of the Nik Color Efex pro filters.', '2006-11-17 17:28:47.000000', NULL, 0),
